{{Codex|The Lato is a highly accurate pistol used by the Tenno everywhere.}}The '''Lato''' is a standard issue pistol for new [[Tenno]] recruits. While its damage suffers, its good accuracy and stability as well as fast reload allows easy handling of the weapon.

This weapon can be sold for {{cc|2,500}}, it is also a [[weapon crafting ingredient]] for {{Weapon|Bolto}}.
{{Checklist|nocategory=true|
* {{Weapon|Lato}} → {{Weapon|Bolto}}<br><small>1st Bolto required for [[Akbolto]]</small>
* {{Weapon|Lato}} → {{Weapon|Bolto}}<br><small>2nd Bolto required for [[Akbolto]]</small>
* {{Weapon|Lato}} → {{Weapon|Bolto}}<br><small>3rd Bolto required for [[Hystrix]]</small>
}}

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals primarily {{D|Slash}} damage.

{{Advantages|}}
{{Disadvantages|}}

{{WeaponComparison|Lato Prime}}
{{WeaponComparison|Lato Vandal|header=n}}
==Acquisition==
During [[Awakening]], the Lato is one of two secondary weapons offered to the player, the other being the {{Weapon|Kunai}}.

The weapon can also be purchased from the [[Market]] for {{cc|10,000}}.

==Incarnon Genesis==
{{Transclude|Lato Incarnon Genesis#Acquisition}}

{{Transclude|Lato Incarnon Genesis#Incarnon Genesis}}

==Tips==
*The Lato has a high chance of [[Slash Damage#Dismemberment|cutting corpses into pieces]], making it a prime candidate for a [[Desecrate|Desecrating]] {{WF|Nekros}} to bring along, as the game considers the cut corpses as separate entities, essentially giving multiple corpses to desecrate from a single enemy and thus yielding more chances to create more drops.
*Once the weapon ranks up to 30, consider using it to build the {{Weapon|Bolto}} which is significantly better, at least in terms of combating armored enemies.

==Trivia==
*The Lato was originally intended to fit in more with the other wood and metal aesthetic Tenno weapons have, its original design can [[:File:FRAGMENT_09_ARCHAIC_WEAPONS.png|seen be seen in this concept art (top right)]]. The {{Weapon|Lato Prime}} is still based on that old design.
**Additionally the Lato was visually reworked in [[Update 19]] and its default skin changed from black and metal grey to the black white red color scheme of Excalibur.
*This weapon is used by the Grineer [[Lancer]]s in [[Vor's Prize]] as a low damage alternative to the {{Weapon|Grakata}}s they normally wield. It is also used by them in [[Mastery Rank]] Promotion Tests. 
*The Lato received a buff to its damage and critical stats in {{ver|14}} to bring it in line with the new MK1 weapons. The {{Weapon|Aklato}} however did not receive this buff until {{ver|15.16}}.
*It was seen in the Dark Sector original concept video.
*Though the word ''[[wiktionary:Lato|Lato]]'' has a variety of meanings in different languages, the usage here may be in Italian where it means "side", a nod to the weapon itself being a sidearm.
*Lato means "summer" in Polish.

