[[File:LatronPrimeXP.png|thumb|189x189px|The Lato Prime with non-Prime colors as a log-in rewards icon.]]
*Written along the side of the barrel is "Evolution", in [[Orokin Language|Orokin script]].
*As of {{ver|10.2}}, all parts of this weapon can be customized.
*Previously, a Lato Prime with the normal {{Weapon|Lato}} default colors and without gold trim could be seen as the image for the ''Secondary Weapons Item XP'' prize on the daily [[Login Rewards]] (albeit rarely), replacing the usual image for the reward.
*The Lato Prime bears a resemblance to the real life [[wikipedia:Derringer|Derringer]] pocket pistol.
*Against their agreement with [[Digital Extremes]], [[wikipedia:Perfect World (company)|Perfect World]] re-released the Lato Prime as part of a [[wikipedia:Halloween|Halloween]] promotion for the [[WARFRAME (China)|Chinese build]] of the game.<ref>[https://forums.warframe.com/topic/711681-perfect-world-is-selling-the-lato-prime/?page=3#comment-7952785 Perfect World is Selling the Lato Prime - &#91;DE&#93;Rebecca's reply]</ref> Between October 28 and October 31, 2016, anyone who purchased the 4,250 Platinum bundle also received the Lato Prime, [[Armor_(Cosmetic)#Seasonal|Dullahan Mask]], {{Weapon|Lacera}}, {{M|Constitution}}, and {{M|Primed Target Cracker}}. The promotion was modified on the 29<sup>th</sup> to give the {{Weapon|Reaper Prime}} instead.
*A hologram of the Lato Prime can be seen in the Arsenal terminal in the Scarlet Spear Flotilla Relay.
*Despite an akimbo variant existing for the base Lato, no {{Weapon|Aklato}} Prime currently exists. This is likely due to the weapon's Founder exclusivity.

